{{ define "home/index" }}
{{ template "layouts/head" dict "Title" "gofs" }}
<main>
	<h1>gofs</h1>
	<p>
		A Go server rendering pages with <code>html/template</code>. The header above is declarative shadow DOM:
		the server renders the markup, the browser attaches it, and no JavaScript is involved.
	</p>

	<section class="card">
		<h2>Examples</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><a href="/contacts">Contacts</a> — search, paging, and inline edit and delete with plain forms</li>
			<li><a href="/contacts/new">New contact</a> — a plain form post with server-side validation</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="card">
		<h2>How it fits together</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><code>internal/server/routes.go</code> — every route in one place</li>
			<li><code>internal/ui/app/pages/&lt;section&gt;/</code> — templates and their handlers, side by side</li>
			<li><code>internal/ui/app/components/&lt;tag&gt;/</code> — shadow DOM markup; behavior, if any, is an inline module script in the same file</li>
			<li><code>internal/ui/app/layouts.gohtml</code> — the document head and foot</li>
			<li><code>internal/app/contact</code> — the backend package: domain rules and the store</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<p>
		The contacts page renders each row with its edit form already in the markup. The list is a declarative
		shadow DOM component; the module script in that file hides the forms until Edit is pressed. Without
		JavaScript they stay visible and the forms still post normally.
	</p>

	<p>
		Dialogs and popovers need no component either. The native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> and the popover
		attributes handle focus, the Escape key and the backdrop themselves.
	</p>

	<section class="card">
		<button type="button" popovertarget="example-popover">Open popover</button>
	</section>

	<div id="example-popover" popover>
		<h2>Hello</h2>
		<p>A native popover: light dismiss, Escape and focus are handled by the browser.</p>
		<button type="button" popovertarget="example-popover" popovertargetaction="hide">Close</button>
	</div>
</main>
{{ template "layouts/foot" . }}
{{ end }}